# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Osmira (awg2-client) — repository ignore rules.
# Everything that is a SECRET, a large local toolchain, or a build artifact
# stays OUT of version control. Only the app source + build scripts ship.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── SECRETS — never publish (leaking these lets anyone sign fake updates) ──
# Release signing keystore and its passwords:
**/key.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pepk
# Google/Firebase service files, if ever added:
**/google-services.json
**/GoogleService-Info.plist
*.serviceaccount.json

# ── Example / user VPN configs (embed WireGuard PRIVATE KEYS) ──
*.vpn
*.conf

# ── Local Go toolchain, module cache and patched GOROOT (hundreds of MB) ──
.gohome/
.gomodcache/
.goroot-patched/

# ── Native build staging + third-party sources fetched for building .so ──
# (amneziawg-go / amneziawg-android are cloned here on demand — see README)
/staging/
/refs/

# ── Build logs ──
*.log

# ── Flutter / Dart / Gradle build output & caches ──
app/build/
app/.dart_tool/
app/.flutter-plugins
app/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
app/.pub-cache/
app/.pub/
app/**/generated_plugin_registrant.*
app/android/.gradle/
app/android/local.properties
app/android/app/debug/
app/android/app/profile/
app/android/app/release/
app/**/*.iml
app/.idea/

# ── OS / editor cruft ──
.DS_Store
*.swp
.vscode/
